question_text:
The following change is made to `pkg/iter/v2/interface.go` in the `grafana/loki` repository:

```go
// Before
type CloseIterator[T any] interface {
	Iterator[T]
	Close() error
}

// After
type CloseIterator[T any] interface {
	Iterator[T]
	Close() error
	// Context returns the context associated with this iterator, if any.
	// Implementations that do not carry a context should return context.Background().
	Context() context.Context
}
```

Because `pkg/iter/iterator.go` defines:

```go
type EntryIterator StreamIterator[logproto.Entry]
type SampleIterator StreamIterator[logproto.Sample]
```

and `StreamIterator[T]` embeds `v2.CloseIterator[T]`, every concrete type that satisfies `EntryIterator` or `SampleIterator` must now also implement `Context() context.Context`. No other files are changed.

Which files within the `grafana/loki` repository would fail to compile as a result of this change? List each file by its path relative to the repository root.
